却是一怔，只见应该离开这里的少女，竟自然的跟着那些丫鬟婆子来来回回接替帮忙。当看到她出来，才动作一僵，露出局促不安的表情：“我……我只是想帮点忙……”李妈妈忍不住眼睛一酸，这孩子原本也是嫡女……若不是钟家惹上那等官司，也不至于……说到底是大爷无情，宠着刘姨娘，见钟家败落，竟抬刘姨娘做奶奶，连亲生女儿都不顾。这好好的嫡女，成了谁都不管，又身份尴尬的存在。李妈妈叹气，终是对着柳蓉唤道：“蓉姐儿，你是懂事的孩子，大夫我不能帮你请，我记得你刚才说给些麻黄也可以是吗？”柳蓉赶忙点头，小小的脸仰着，满是期待。李妈妈心中又是一酸，赶忙撇过头，对着身旁的二等丫鬟吩咐道：“小翠，你领蓉姐儿去我屋中，取些我给我家那口子准备的药，我记得里面就有麻黄。”说完略迟疑，又加了一句：“里面还有些补药，你也一并给蓉姐儿取些。”一旁的小翠眉头皱起：“这事情要是给大奶奶知道了，怕是……”“没事，大房如今为了九小姐选秀的事情发愁，没时间管到二房。”蓉姐儿赶忙对着李妈妈感激的点头，直到李妈妈转身继续忙碌，才随着翠儿往丫鬟婆子们住的厢房去。只是走得远了，翠儿的脚步却是越来越慢，蓉姐儿眉头微微紧了紧，却是不动声色的继续跟着。待得到了偏僻地儿，翠儿才停下脚步，面带厌恶的看向柳蓉：“蓉姐儿，容奴婢说句不中听的。还请您以后莫再往二房跑了，您这样，且不说会不会让二房、大房不合，却会累的李妈妈难做人。”“如今这府邸里谁不知道太夫人最疼刘大奶奶，您自己也清楚，因为你母亲在，才让太夫人委屈自己的外孙女做了多年侧室，您就算不为二房和李妈妈考虑，也请不要再害我们这帮做丫鬟的了！”翠儿越说越尖锐，脸上的厌恶也更不加掩饰。还当自己是嫡女呢，不过一个身份尴尬的庶女罢了。也不知道少生事端，李妈妈也是，这么做事，万一被蓉姐儿赖上，到时候开罪了大奶奶，这侯府还能呆吗？看来她得赶紧想想办法分配远一些，免得到时候被牵连。“我明白，这是最后一次。”正当翠儿心里计较着，便听之前一直沉默的蓉姐儿，竟是认认真真的开口了。翠儿忍不住低头，便对上一双略带嘲讽却晶莹闪亮的眼睛，在这眼神前，她竟有种被看透的感觉，不禁心虚别过头，一时间连柳蓉回话的语气异常平淡，和之前判若两人都不曾发现。翠儿别过头后一愣，她这是怎么了，竟被一个胆小若鼠的庶女的眼神看得不知所措。只是，蓉姐儿怎么可能有那样的眼神！翠儿赶忙再次看向蓉姐儿，便见那一双杏眼依旧怯弱，哪有之前一瞬间的锐利。果然是瞧错了，若三姑娘不是被大奶奶养的和她的性子一样柔弱，刘姨娘又哪会这般容易被抬正。想到此，翠儿对眼前这府里的三小姐越加不屑，不再多说什么，领着柳蓉继续向前走。望着翠儿的背影，柳蓉好看的眉头皱起。真是墙倒众人推，若是钟氏依旧是大奶奶，又有谁敢这么对她，不过这翠儿虽然讨厌，有些话却是中规中矩的，李妈妈毕竟只是掌事妈妈，若只是因为心善帮她，而被牵连就不好了，看来要想想其它办法弄药才是！只是她到这个世界，才几日光景，即便空有一身医术，好吧，是拿刀子的技术，在这个连卫生防卫都不健全的世界也没什么用。这个时代谁敢要外科大夫开刀？如此也就无法利用自己的能力帮助那个为了她弄的重病的便宜母亲。最后竟是沦落到只能利用平时都不大注意的中药，来帮助这身体的母亲治疗。还要这样装傻充愣的弄药！只是现在连这一点恐怕也不能继续了。偏偏她还担心旁人瞧出破绽，对很多事情不敢细问。无法找出更好的办法。而真心对她的母亲，在她身体稍好的时候，便染了风寒，体虚的只能卧床，她也不好让对方再担忧。不过即便如此，还是从旁人的闲言碎语中了解到一些。她母亲钟氏，是柳府大爷嫡妻，却因为娘家参与储争败落灭门，柳家为免被牵连，便废了钟氏，抬了原本的刘姨娘，也就是太夫人外孙女为正妻。没了娘家的依靠，夫家又当她是蛇蝎，所以钟氏的日子异常难过。屋漏偏逢连夜雨，这身体前些日子也不知为何就失足掉进了莲花池，这大冷的天，却是叫她差点丧命，还好有家丁路过，这才救起。就是这样，也是昏迷了三天三夜才醒过来。只是外人不知，这身体的主人，早就去了，现在不过是鸠占鹊巢罢了。好笑的是，她落水，不好好救治也就罢了，竟还将她落水的责任放到钟氏身上，将钟氏和奄奄一息的她一道从上好的梅园迁出，硬生生的让她们搬到了离柴房不远的偏房。做这事的人何其歹毒，这分明就是要她死。还好有钟氏在，若不是钟氏日夜不离守护，硬生生的守了三天三夜，她恐怕也到不了这身躯壳里，只是她醒了，钟氏却累得昏迷。母爱如此，即便为的不是她，受到好处的却是她，她无乱如何也要治好这身体的母亲的。只是越这样对比，她便越忍不住对那些狠心的人咬牙切齿。更是对这府邸里，到现在还不曾见过的大爷，也就是她所谓的父亲厌恶至极。“这是麻黄，赶紧拿了回去。”翠儿取了药，面色冷硬，完全不提李妈妈说的，还要给她的补药。柳蓉微不可见的皱眉，眼角余光却是瞥见翠儿放在背后的手里，拎着一个药包。“还不赶紧回去，是麻黄也不打算要了吗？”翠儿见柳蓉看向自己身后，眉头皱起。柳蓉默默的接过麻黄，就在翠儿嘴角扬起一丝笑意之时，却是突然抬头对着翠儿甜甜一笑，天真的指着从翠儿身侧漏出的药包开口：“李妈妈真好，二奶奶身边缺人，还担心我人小拿不动药，让翠儿姐姐帮我提药。”“你说什么呢……”柳蓉完全不管翠儿开口，顾自将小脸绷紧变得认真严肃，小大人般继续道：“我不能这么不懂事，我和翠儿姐姐一起回去，回去给李妈妈帮忙。”说着，提着东西就向来的方向走去，翠儿一愣，随即一惊，若是叫李妈妈知道她克扣药物，这还得了，赶忙拦住柳蓉。“李妈妈那边不用你帮忙，自有借的丫鬟会帮忙。”“不行，李妈妈对我这么好，还让翠儿你替我拿着补药，送我回去，我怎么能顾自回去，我一定要去帮李妈妈的忙。”说着不顾翠儿的阻拦，要继续向前走。翠儿见拦不住柳蓉，脸上的镇定终于挂不住，赶忙将手中的药包塞入柳蓉手中：“钟姨娘毕竟病着，身体重，需要人照顾，你还是拿着药赶紧先回去照顾吧，李妈妈那边有我呢，我就不亲自送你回去了。”柳蓉嘴角微微勾起：“这如何好意思，二奶奶要生，正是忙的时候，李妈妈这会一个人恐怕忙不过来。”“我回去帮衬着也就忙的过来了，你赶紧回去吧。”说着话，也不等柳蓉继续开口，赶忙转身快步往回走，就仿佛后面追了个大虫一般。“那便谢谢翠儿姐姐了，还要麻烦翠儿姐姐帮我和李妈妈说声谢谢。”望着远远听到自己的声音，又加快几步的翠儿，柳蓉露出一个得意的笑容，提着药心满意足的往回走。却说两人离开后，两人身后的梅树后竟走出一个一身白衣锦袍，腰上缀着一枚五爪金龙玉佩的少年，只见他满脸玩味的看着柳蓉离开的方向。", "source": "www.quanwenyuedu.io", "source_url": "https://www.quanwenyuedu.io/n/houmenyinu/1.html", "_fixed": true, "content_en": "Chapter 1 Asking for Medicine The snow had just stopped, and a thick layer of snow had accumulated in the pear garden. The maid and her mother-in-law walked in and out quickly with a nervous look on their faces, making the snow crunch under their feet. \"If you move faster, the second grandma is about to give birth. Everyone must pay attention and the hot water is ready. Is Po Wen here?\" the housekeeper asked eagerly. \"Not yet, we have sent someone to invite him! The second master will be back soon.\" Following the housekeeper's words, the atmosphere in the yard became more tense, and the maid carrying hot water trotted forward. At this moment, a girl in a small fine cloth jacket, with a sallow complexion and a bun on her head, who looked to be at most ten years old, timidly approached the housekeeper: \"Mama Li, I... my mother is sick, can you help me hire a doctor... or... give me some ephedra...\" At the end of the sentence, her voice became quieter and quieter, almost inaudible, and only those watery almond eyes looked at Mother Li timidly. Mother Li frowned: \"Go back quickly, Second Grandma is about to give birth now, and no one has time to care about your troubles. If you accidentally delay things here, don't use Grandma. Grandma can't spare you.\" After saying this, she caught a glimpse of a little maid who accidentally dropped the cotton strip used to wipe Second Mistress when she gave birth to the ground. Mother Li stepped forward quickly: \"Why are you so careless? Come on, go to the room and get some more. Don't delay. These are all things that will be used later.\" \"We don't have enough manpower to begin with, and something like this happened. We have to quickly ask someone to borrow people from other courtyards...\" After saying this, Mother Li turned and left without looking at the girl who was frozen at the side. After a while, Mrs. Wen arrived. She hurriedly welcomed her into the house. She didn't walk out of the house until she started delivering the baby and continued to supervise. When he saw the scene in the courtyard, he was startled. He saw that the girl who should have left here naturally followed the maids and women back and forth to take over the help. When he saw her coming out, his movements froze and he showed an embarrassed expression: \"I... I just want to help...\" Mother Li couldn't help but her eyes were sore. This child was originally a legitimate daughter... If the Zhong family hadn't been involved in such a lawsuit, it wouldn't have happened... In the final analysis, it was the uncle who was ruthless and doted on Aunt Liu. Seeing the decline of the Zhong family, he raised Aunt Liu to be his grandmother, even ignoring his own daughter. This good legitimate daughter has become an existence that no one cares about and her status is embarrassing. Mother Li sighed and finally called to Liu Rong: \"Sister Rong, you are a sensible child. I can't help you get a doctor. I remember you just said you could give me some ephedra, right?\" Liu Rong nodded quickly, her little face looking up, full of expectation. Mother Li felt sour again. She quickly turned her head and told the second-class maid next to her: \"Xiao Cui, take Sister Rong to my room and get some medicine I prepared for my house. I remember there is ephedra in it.\" After speaking, he hesitated and added: \"There are some tonics in it. You can also get some for Sister Rong.\" Next to her, Xiao Cui frowned: \"If grandma finds out about this, I'm afraid...\" \"It's okay, the first house is worried about Miss Ninth's talent show right now, and has no time to take care of the second bedroom.\" Sister Rong hurriedly nodded gratefully to Mother Li, until Mother Li turned around to continue her work, and then followed Cui'er to the side room where the maids and ladies lived. As they walked further, Cui'er's steps became slower and slower. Sister Rong's brows tightened slightly, but she continued to follow calmly. When they reached a remote place, Cui'er stopped and looked at Liu Rong with disgust: \"Sister Rong, I don't want to hear what I say. Please don't run to the second room again. If you do this, not to mention whether it will make it difficult for Mother Li, who is not compatible with the second room and the first room, but will be tired, to be a good person.\" \"Who knows in this mansion now? Mrs. Dao loves Grandma Liu the most, and you know it yourself. It is because of your mother's presence that Mrs. Dao has wronged her granddaughter to be the concubine for many years. Even if you don't think about the second wife and Mother Li, please don't harm us maids anymore!\" Cui'er became more and more pointed, and the disgust on her face became more undisguised. She still thinks that she is a legitimate daughter, but she is just a concubine with an embarrassing status. I don’t know if Shao Sheng will cause trouble, and the same goes for Li’s mother. If Sister Rong takes advantage of her and offends Grandma, can she still stay in the Hou Mansion? It seemed that she had to quickly think of a way to distribute things further away to avoid being implicated in the future. \"I understand, this is the last time.\" Just as Cui'er was calculating in her mind, Sister Rong, who had been silent before, actually spoke seriously. Cui'er couldn't help but lower her head, and met a pair of slightly mocking but sparkling eyes. In front of these eyes, she felt like she was being seen through. She couldn't help but look away with a guilty conscience. For a while, even Liu Rong's tone of reply was unusually bland, completely different from before, neither of them noticed. Cui'er turned away and was stunned. What was wrong with her? She was so confused by the eyes of a timid concubine. But, how could Sister Rong have such a look in her eyes! Cui'er hurriedly looked at Sister Rong again, and saw that her almond-shaped eyes were still timid, not as sharp as the previous moment. Sure enough, she was wrong. If the third girl hadn't been raised by the eldest grandmother and was as weak as her temperament, Aunt Liu would not have been promoted so easily. Thinking of this, Cui'er became more and more disdainful of the third young lady in the mansion in front of her. She said nothing more and led Liu Rong forward. Looking at Cui'er's back, Liu Rong frowned. It's really overwhelming. If Mrs. Zhong is still the eldest grandmother, who would dare to treat her like this? But although this Cui'er is annoying, some of her words are quite satisfactory. After all, Mrs. Li is just the mother in charge. It would be bad if she was implicated just because she was kind-hearted. It seems that she has to think of other ways to get the medicine! It's just that she has only been in this world for a few days. Even if she has medical skills, well, the skill of holding a knife, it is of little use in this world where even health defense is not perfect. Who dares to ask a surgeon to perform an operation in this day and age? like", "translated": true, "title_en": "Chapter 1"}